---
// DBAS: the two ideas behind the installation, and the design move each
// one became. McLuhan is a public-domain photograph (Bernard Gotfryd,
// 1967, Library of Congress, via Wikimedia Commons): McLuhan leaning on a
// television showing McLuhan, the medium made visible. Baudrillard has no
// public-domain photo, so his idea is drawn instead, as a small Bauhaus
// poster: a mesh of thin connections, everyone a "switching centre", and
// one thick line through it, one call. Ideas from the thesis, ch. 3.2.
---

<figure class="theory wide">
	<div class="theory-grid">
		<section class="theory-card">
			<picture>
				<source srcset="/images/dbas/theory/mcluhan-tv-1967.webp" type="image/webp" />
				<img src="/images/dbas/theory/mcluhan-tv-1967.jpg" width="872" height="1024" alt="Marshall McLuhan in 1967, arms folded, leaning on a television set that shows his own face." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
			</picture>
			<div class="theory-text">
				<p class="theory-quote">The medium is the message.</p>
				<p class="theory-who">Marshall McLuhan, <cite>Understanding Media</cite>, 1964</p>
				<p class="theory-idea">We notice what a medium carries and forget the medium itself. McLuhan asks us to make it perceptible again.</p>
				<p class="theory-move"><span>So</span> the weight of the handset and the resistance of the dial stay. They are how you feel the medium.</p>
			</div>
		</section>
		<section class="theory-card">
			<svg class="theory-poster" viewBox="0 0 300 352" role="img" aria-label="A drawn poster: a dense mesh of thin lines between many small dots, with one thick blue line cutting across it between two larger circles.">
				<rect width="300" height="352" class="p-bg" />
				{Array.from({ length: 22 }, (_, i) => {
					const pts = Array.from({ length: 22 }, (_, j) => [20 + ((j * 97 + 13) % 260), 30 + ((j * 53 + 29) % 230)]);
					const [x1, y1] = pts[i];
					const [x2, y2] = pts[(i * 7 + 3) % 22];
					const [x3, y3] = pts[(i * 5 + 11) % 22];
					return (
						<g>
							<line class="p-thin" x1={x1} y1={y1} x2={x2} y2={y2} />
							<line class="p-thin" x1={x1} y1={y1} x2={x3} y2={y3} />
							<circle class="p-node" cx={x1} cy={y1} r="3" />
						</g>
					);
				})}
				<line class="p-call" x1="38" y1="236" x2="262" y2="58" />
				<circle class="p-end" cx="38" cy="236" r="11" />
				<circle class="p-end" cx="262" cy="58" r="11" />
				<text class="p-title" x="20" y="300">THE ECSTASY OF</text>
				<text class="p-title" x="20" y="326">COMMUNICATION</text>
			</svg>
			<div class="theory-text">
				<p class="theory-quote">We become switching centres.</p>
				<p class="theory-who">After Jean Baudrillard, <cite>The Ecstasy of Communication</cite></p>
				<p class="theory-idea">Everything is immediate and exposed. Distance, delay and absence collapse, and so does meaning.</p>
				<p class="theory-move"><span>So</span> the delay comes back: a slow dial, one call at a time, and the chance nobody answers.</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
	<figcaption>McLuhan photographed by Bernard Gotfryd, 1967 (Library of Congress, public domain). The Baudrillard poster is drawn for this page.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.theory { margin-block: var(--space-6); }
	.theory-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--space-5); }
	@media (min-width: 760px) { .theory-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--space-6); } }
	.theory-card { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; gap: var(--space-3); }
	.theory-card img, .theory-poster { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 300 / 352; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 0; }
	.p-bg { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 3; }
	.p-thin { stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: .6; opacity: .45; }
	.p-node { fill: var(--ink); }
	.p-call { stroke: var(--blue); stroke-width: 7; }
	.p-end { fill: var(--blue); }
	.p-title { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 22px; letter-spacing: .02em; fill: var(--ink); }
	.theory-text { display: grid; gap: var(--space-1); align-content: start; }
	.theory-quote { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-body); font-style: italic; font-size: var(--fs-h3); line-height: 1.3; color: var(--ink); }
	.theory-who { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--muted); }
	.theory-who cite { font-style: italic; }
	.theory-idea { margin: var(--space-2) 0 0; font-size: var(--fs-small); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--body); }
	.theory-move { margin: var(--space-2) 0 0; padding-top: var(--space-2); border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); font-size: var(--fs-small); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink); }
	.theory-move span { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; margin-right: .3em; }
	.theory figcaption { margin-top: var(--space-3); font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--muted); }
</style>
